<p>
    This incident is shown because of {{ incident.getFailureEventsCount() }} PHP exception(s)
    of type {{ incident.getFirstEvent().getClass() }} and {{ incident.getFirstEvent().getCode() }} code.
    {% if incident.getFailureEventsCount() > 200 %}
        <br />
        Only the first 200 events are displayed to preserve performances
    {% endif %}
</p>

<p>
    First exception information:
    <table class="table table-bordered">
        <tr>
            <td>Class</td><td>{{ incident.getFirstEvent().getClass() }}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Message</td><td>{{ incident.getFirstEvent().getMessage() }}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Code</td><td>{{ incident.getFirstEvent().getCode() }}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>File</td><td>{{ incident.getFirstEvent().getFile() }}</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Line</td><td>{{ incident.getFirstEvent().getLine() }}</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    Exceptions log:
    <table class="table table-bordered">
        <tr>
            <td>Date</td>
            <td>Message</td>
            <td>Trace</td>
        </tr>
        {% set count = 0 %}
        {% for exception in incident.getEvents() if count < 200 %}
            {% set count = count + 1 %}
            <tr>
                <td>{{ exception.getDateCreated()|date }}</td>
                <td>{{ exception.getMessage() }}</td>
                <td>
                    <a class="btn btn-primary" ng-href="#/server/incidents/event/{{ exception.getId() }}" href="#/server/incidents/event/{{ exception.getId() }}">
                        View more
                    </a>
                </td>
            </tr>
        {% endfor %}
    </table>
</p>

<p>
    If exception description doesn't give you enough information to solve it or you think it's caused by DeskPRO code
    issue, you can report this error to DeskPRO.
</p>
